    "reason": "[ev-89034c5d2c74] says that Direct-Server-Return service connections established before Cilium v1.13.3 will be disrupted and need to be re-established. With the same configuration, the DSR datapath now handles those older connections differently, so behavior-changed fits. The subject is wire-level Direct-Server-Return handling, so protocol-behavior \"direct-server-return\" is the right family and name. Re-establishing the connections is what the operator has to do afterwards; the evidence does not describe a separate migration step, so the migration-required framing does not fit better.",
